From 20b1d6a201361b3796f05a56565f44ee5bbcdb8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:33:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Genesis GOLD ledger: paid-mint holds settled from
 finalized chain facts

Port the Genesis paid-mint GOLD book from the Sepolia rehearsal into the
World Worker, exposed only to the Genesis signer through the GenesisGold
service binding (WorkerEntrypoint). The production registry is empty until
the mainnet contract is deployed, so every hold is refused for now.

- Bounded log search: only the order window [deadline-900-120s, deadline],
  in eth_getLogs requests of at most 10 blocks (Alchemy Free).
- Registry entries name their domain version and recipient; addresses and
  code hash are normalized (pinnedDeployment).
- Cron: Genesis step isolated, pages of 8, one bytecode check per finalized
  block (cpu_ms 50), a malformed entry never stops the others.
- Migration 0022: genesis_gold_cursors.

server/world-gold.ts (wallet lock) changes by one type line; the lock hash
is not updated, so wallet-lock fails until a new Swarm audit and the
owner's approval.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
